ok   loopback? is 127.0.0.0/8, ::1 and IPv4-mapped 127.x.x.x
ok   loopback? is false for every other address
ok   without a trusted proxy client_ip is the peer, whatever X-Forwarded-For says
ok   with a trusted proxy a loopback peer's last X-Forwarded-For hop is the client
ok   with a trusted proxy a peer that is not loopback keeps its own address
ok   a last hop that is empty, too long or not printable ASCII falls back to the peer
ok   Request.trusted_proxy is false until set
ok   Config#trusted_proxy comes from CYBERTRAIN_TRUSTED_PROXY (1 or true)
ok   a peer inside a trusted IPv4 CIDR names the client; one outside does not
ok   a single trusted address matches only itself
ok   IPv6 trusted networks: compressed, zone ignored on the peer, bounded prefixes
ok   Request.trusted_proxies is empty until set and refuses a bad entry
ok   the loopback shorthand and the list add up
ok   IpAddress.parse_network bounds prefixes and refuses what is not a network
ok   Config#trusted_proxies comes from CYBERTRAIN_TRUSTED_PROXIES and is checked at boot
15 tests, 127 assertions, 0 failures
